          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What payment terms should small businesses expect from clothing manufacturers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Standard payment terms are 30% deposit upon order confirmation and 70% balance before shipment. New small businesses rarely receive net terms (payment after delivery) until establishing trust through multiple successful orders. Letters of Credit provide security for orders over $50,000 but add bank fees. Avoid manufacturers demanding 100% upfront payment, which indicates potential fraud or financial instability."
          }
